---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — **한 편을 빼면 답이 얼마나 움직이나.** (`/one-out`)
 *
 * ── 왜 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *   8/15 에 같은 자료로 답 둘을 냈고, 작품을 35 → 59 로 늘리자 하나는 그대로였고
 *   하나는 3분의 1 이 됐다. 그날 두 번째 정정을 냈다.
 *   ⭐⭐ **늘려 보기 전에 알 수 있었다.** 가진 표본에서 한 편씩 빼 보기만 하면 됐다.
 *
 * ── ⛔ 이 지면이 지키는 것 ────────────────────────────────────
 * ⛔ **「흔들린다」를 「틀렸다」로 안 적는다.** 흔들리는 답은 아직 답이 아닌 것이지 거짓이 아니다.
 * ⛔ **사분위 폭을 자로 안 쓴다.** 두 답이 1.5배 대 1.8배로 **거의 같아 보인다** —
 *    사분위가 이상값을 밖에 두고 안 보기 때문이다. 그 실패를 지면에 그대로 싣는다.
 * ⛔ **우리 기사를 예로 든다.** 남의 것을 잡는 지면이 아니다.
 * ⛔ 광고 자리를 만들지 않는다. Riot Production(App 866800) 승인 전이다.
 *
 * 🔴 Astro 앞말(`---` 사이)은 **TypeScript 다.** JSX 를 넣으면 빌드가 죽는다.
 * 🔴 앞말에서 `export function` 을 쓰지 않는다 — Astro 가 딴 스코프로 옮긴다.
 * 🔴 JSX 는 끝 공백을 버린다. 붙여 써야 할 곳은 `{' '}` 를 넣는다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import KcwRelatedArticles from '../../components/KcwRelatedArticles.astro';
import KcwCardnews from '../../components/KcwCardnews.astro';
import KcwShorts from '../../components/KcwShorts.astro';
import d from '../../data/wikitip-one-out.json';

const 단단 = d.findings.find((f) => f.atFirstPublication.verdict?.steady);
const 흔들 = d.findings.find((f) => f.atFirstPublication.verdict?.steady === false);
const 몫 = (v: number, u: string) => `${v}${u === 'per cent' ? '%' : ''}`;

const TITLE = 'We published two findings and corrected one. A one-line check told them apart before we knew';
const DESC =
  'Removing a single title from our sample left one median exactly where it was and moved the '
  + 'other by 89% of itself. The interquartile range put the two within a whisker of each other.';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/'],
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd}
  canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/one-out">
  <h1>{TITLE}</h1>
  <p class="lead">{d.question}</p>
  <p class="q">
    Yes. Take the numbers behind a median, remove one, recompute. Do it once for every number. On
    the day we published, the finding that survived did not move at all when any single title was
    removed. The one we corrected moved by {흔들?.atFirstPublication.oneOut.swingOverMedian} times
    its own size.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>The two findings, on the day we published them</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Finding</th><th>Titles</th><th>Median</th><th>Range without any one title</th>
            <th>Swing ÷ median</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {d.findings.map((f) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="nm">{f.what}</td>
              <td>{f.atFirstPublication.n}</td>
              <td>{몫(f.atFirstPublication.oneOut.median, f.unit)}</td>
              <td>
                {몫(f.atFirstPublication.oneOut.lowestWithoutOne, f.unit)} to
                {' '}{몫(f.atFirstPublication.oneOut.highestWithoutOne, f.unit)}
              </td>
              <td>{f.atFirstPublication.oneOut.swingOverMedian}×</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      The half-life median sat at {단단?.atFirstPublication.oneOut.median} months and stayed at
      {' '}{단단?.atFirstPublication.oneOut.median} months no matter which of the
      {' '}{단단?.atFirstPublication.n} titles was dropped. Nothing in the sample was holding it up.
      The floor-change median could be pushed anywhere between
      {' '}{몫(흔들?.atFirstPublication.oneOut.lowestWithoutOne, 흔들?.unit)} and
      {' '}{몫(흔들?.atFirstPublication.oneOut.highestWithoutOne, 흔들?.unit)} by removing one of
      five. We reported it anyway.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What happened next</h2>
    <p>
      We widened the set from 35 titles to 59 for an unrelated reason. Here is where the same two
      medians landed.
    </p>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Finding</th><th>Then</th><th>Now</th><th>Titles then → now</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {d.findings.map((f) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="nm">{f.what}</td>
              <td>{몫(f.atFirstPublication.oneOut.median, f.unit)}</td>
              <td>{몫(f.now.oneOut.median, f.unit)}</td>
              <td class="fine">{f.atFirstPublication.n} → {f.now.n}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      One held to the number. The other fell to a third of what we had published, and we corrected
      the article that carried it — the second correction on that piece that day. The check would
      have cost one line and it would have told us which was which.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The check we would normally have reached for does not work here</h2>
    <p>
      The interquartile range is the usual way to describe spread, and on these two samples it says
      they are almost the same.
    </p>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Finding</th><th>IQR ÷ median</th><th>Leave-one-out swing ÷ median</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {d.findings.map((f) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="nm">{f.what}</td>
              <td>{f.atFirstPublication.iqr?.overMedian ?? '—'}×</td>
              <td>{f.atFirstPublication.oneOut.swingOverMedian}×</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>{d.method.whyNotIqr}</p>
    <p class="note">
      The five values behind that first publication were −27.8, −16.9, −6.7, −5.0 and +60.2. The
      interquartile range is computed from the middle of that list and never has to look at +60.2
      at all. Leave-one-out asks what the answer becomes when +60.2 is the one taken away, which
      is exactly the question a small sample raises.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How to run it</h2>
    <p>{d.method.how}</p>
    <p class="note">
      {d.method.noRandomness} We call it {d.method.name} rather than by its statistical name
      because the name is the whole method. Our threshold is {d.method.threshold} — a median that
      moves by half its own size when one observation leaves is not yet a finding.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What this page cannot tell you</h2>
    {d.cannotSay.map((s) => <p class="note">{s}</p>)}
  </section>

  <KcwCardnews set="oneout" count={5} />

  <KcwShorts set="oneout"
    says={`A man and a woman read out what happened to each of two medians when a single title `
      + `was removed.`} />

  <KcwRelatedArticles page="/one-out" />
</WikiTip>
